* r68 strips single quotes from a macro argument as it does double ones (TrW 'Q5' with #'\1' in
* the body: 'Q5'; it was made a number first); \' in a macro body is a quote when the body
* expands (TrW \'Q5\'); ifp1 (r68's first pass) is a true conditional (a defs file's ifp1, use,
* endc).
* fixed: 0cc3d11 2026-10-11 r68togas: single-quoted macro arguments; \' in macro bodies; ifp1
* expect text: 3afc5135 3afc6162 3afc5135 3afc6162 3afc0000 3afc0007
TrW MACRO
 move.w #'\1',(a5)+
 endm
TrN MACRO
 move.w #\1,(a5)+
 endm
T2 macro * comment
 TrW \'Q5\'	* a comment
 TrW \'ab\'
 endm
 ifp1
SEVEN equ 7
 endc
 psect macro_quote_args,0,0,0,0,0
 TrW 'Q5'
 TrW ab
 T2
 TrN "cd"
 TrN SEVEN
 ends
